# Data & messaging

https://pisigo.com

## SQL

```go
sqlDB, err := postgres.OpenConfig(postgres.Config{...})
// sqlite.OpenMemory() for tests (single connection)
```

Use `db.SQL`: `Get`, `Select`, `Exec`, `Transaction`. Prefer `db` struct tags for scanning.

Migrations:

```bash
pisigo migrate create add_users
```

```go
m := migrate.New(sqlDB, "migrations")
_ = m.Up(ctx)
```

Files: `-- +migrate Up` / `-- +migrate Down`. Placeholders `?` (auto `$n` on Postgres).

## Store / Queue / PubSub

- Interfaces: `store.Store`, `queue.Queue`, `pubsub.PubSub`
- Local/dev: `adapters/memory`
- Prod cache/rate-limit: `adapters/redis`
- Streams: `adapters/nats` (JetStream queue + core pubsub)

Do not import Redis/NATS from domain code — depend on interfaces.

## Mongo

`mongodb.Open(mongodb.Config{URI, Database})` — separate from `db.SQL`.

## Ops near data

- `health.Ready("db", sqlDB.Ping)`
- Cache responses only for safe GET/HEAD via `middleware.Cache`
